-# UX round 3 (D2/R8) — the section-collapse chevron for .ibox-tools. Pair with
-# ibox_classes(collapsed:) (or a manual `.collapsed` class) on the .ibox so empty sections
-# start collapsed; the glyph direction is CSS-owned (_ibox.scss keys off .ibox.collapsed —
-# always ship fa-chevron-up here).
-# locals: collapsed: (default false)
- collapsed = local_assigns.fetch(:collapsed, false)
-# Investor UX round (2026-07): a QUIET icon control, not button chrome — .btn is reserved
-# for real actions (docs/ui-conventions.md "Links vs buttons"). The CSS glyph swap keys off
-# .ibox.collapsed, so the wrapper change is invisible to the collapse contract.
%a.collapse-link{ role: 'button', tabindex: 0, 'aria-expanded' => (!collapsed).to_s, 'aria-label' => t('shared.ibox_collapse_link.toggle', default: 'Toggle section') }
  %span.ibox-collapse-glyph
    %i.fa.fa-chevron-up{ 'aria-hidden' => 'true' }
